  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 345 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nNorthwest flow continues today into Friday, with H5 zonal flow \ndeveloping later in the day. An upper trough digs into the Pacific \nNorthwest heading into early Saturday, serving to support southwest \nflow into the Northern Plains later in the weekend. Strong warm air \nadvection takes shape Friday into Saturday, ahead of our next cold \nfront. This will allow temperatures to climb well into the 80s in \nthe southern and central Red River Valley, as well as southeast \nNorth Dakota and west central Minnesota. Further north, widespread \nmid to upper 70s are expected. South to southeast winds of 15-25 mph \nare likely Friday afternoon, with gusts up to 35 mph. There will be \na wind shift to the northwest, then north late Saturday into Sunday \nas much cooler air works into the region. Highs on Sunday (in the \n50s to upper 60s) will likely occur very early in the day, with \ntemps falling through the day. Rain chances enter the forecast \nSunday afternoon and remain in the area through Monday afternoon in \nassociation with the cold front.",
